  "course_summary": "ISEN 630 | Human Operator in Complex Systems | Fall 2026\nInstructor: Thomas Ferris | tferris@tamu.edu\nTopics: Lambert's Law, photometry, luminance, reflectance, color-anomalous vision, visual acuity, limits of detection, limits of identification, sound localization, auditory displays, graphical icons, naturally-mapping representations, control mapping, compatibility, written information processing, changing behavior with warnings, HFE methods, design principles for effective display, control design, warning design, noise control, light adaptation, visual correction, color coding, psychology of color, advanced displays, basic control types, documentation, warnings, hearing loss, attention basics, eye anatomy, ear anatomy, retina, rods and cones, refraction, contrast, readable text, color vision, size and depth cues, design for proper illumination, calculating illuminance, displays, controls and dynamics",
